{"id":"word:hebrew:H4054","type":"word","title":"מִגְרָשׁ","subtitle":"H4054 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a suburb (i.e. open country whither flocks are driven from pasture); hence, the area around a building , or the margin of the sea","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מִגְרָשׁ (H4054) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 115 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מִגְרָשׁ (migrâsh) means a suburb (i.e. open country whither flocks are driven from pasture); hence, the area around a building , or the margin of the sea First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 16."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מִגְרָשׁ","transliteration":"migrâsh","pronunciation":"mig-rawsh'","strong":"H4054","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4054","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מִגְרָשֶׁ֑/הָ","מִגְרָשֶֽׁי/הָ","מִגְרָשֶׁ֔/הָ","מִגְרָשֶׁ֔י/הָ","מִגְרָשֶֽׁ/הָ"],"morphs":[["HNcmpc/Sp3fs",90],["HC/Ncmpc/Sp3fp",5],["HNcmpc/Sp3mp",3],["HNcmpc/Sp3fp",3],["HNcmpc",2],["HNcmsc",2],["HNcmsa",2],["HC/Ncmpc/Sp3mp",2],["HNcmpa",1],["HNcmsc/Sp3fs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a suburb (i.e. open country whither flocks are driven from pasture); hence, the area around a building , or the margin of the sea","usage":"cast out, suburb.","full":"H4054. migrash or migrashah מִגְרָשׁ noun masculine Num 35:2 common, common-land, open land (perhaps originally pasture-land , as place of [cattle] driving ) — absolute ׳מ Ezek 45:2 2 t. + 48:15 (Co מגרשָׁהּ ); construct מִגְרַשׁ Lev 25:34 ; 2Chr 31:19 ; (on מִגְרָשָׁהּ Ezek 36:5 compare גרשׁ ); elsewhere plural, absolute מִגְרשׁוֺת 27:28 (Baer); Co מרעשׁת assumed from רָעַשׁ , compare ᵐ5 ; construct מִגְרְשֵׁי Num 35:4 2 t.; suffix מִגְרָשֶׁיהָ Josh 21:13 (twice in verse) + 42 t.; מִגְרָשֶׁהָ 21:11 46t. in Joshua 21 (generally ֑ or ֔ + but also ֖ 21:21 ); מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶם Num 35:3-4 t.; מִגְרְשֵׁיהֶן 35:7-8 t. — common-land , usually plural, and usually as attached to a city or town, especially as surrounding Levitical cities 35:2-3 , 4 , 5 , 7 ; Josh 14:4 ; 21:2 55t. Joshua 21 (all P; in Manuscripts & old Vrss. are two verses Joshua 21, between 21:35 ; 21:36 , with ׳מ 4t.; omitted by Masora, Editions, Baer, but compare Theile, & Di on the passage); 1Chr 6:40 40 t. 1 Chronicles 6; 13:2 ; 2Chr 11:14 ; so also מ ׳שְׂדֵה Lev 25:34 (H), מ ׳שְׂדֵי 2Chr 31:19 ; lands surrounding the holy city Ezek 48:15 , 17 ; open land or space about the temple 45:2 ; only 1Chr 5:16 שָׁרוֺן כלמִֿגְרְשֵׁי of (pasture-) lands in a district, compare שׁרון . — Ezek 27:28 מגרשׁות , if true text, = open country about Tyre (opposed to sea, compare context), but see Da & compare above גֹּרֹתָיו see גּוֺר below II. גור . גשׁם (√ of following; compare Arabic be bulky, massive , body , Syriac id. )","rootNote":"also (in plural) feminine (Ezekiel 27:28) מִגְרָשָׁה ; from 1644 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 5 16","keyReferences":["1Chr 5 16","1Chr 6 40","1Chr 6 42","1Chr 6 42","1Chr 6 43","1Chr 6 43","1Chr 6 44","1Chr 6 44"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":115,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 5 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":5,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִגְרְשֵׁ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 40","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִגְרָשֶׁ֖י/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 42","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִגְרָשֶׁ֑י/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 42","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִגְרָשֶֽׁי/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 43","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":43,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִגְרָשֶׁ֔י/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 43","book"